From 9dbc160504e062031335c78ec0d6f4b3c11baf88 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 19 Sep 2026 09:14:50 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 5/5] Repair navigation off the homepage and the sticky filter
 bar

Search: SiteNavbar renders on ten pages but only Index passes onSearch, and the
anchors it scrolled to exist only there. On the other nine, typing in the search
box did nothing at all - and neither did Regions, Themes or NGO Directory, which
used the same missing anchors. Fall back to navigating to the feed; Index
already reads q/theme/region/country from the URL.

Filter bar: it stuck at top-[88px] under a header measuring 29 + 64 + 40 + 1 =
134px at z-50, so 46px of a ~50px bar sat behind the navbar - invisible in
practice, and any replacement constant would break again when the mobile menu
opens. SiteNavbar now publishes its measured height as --header-h via a
ResizeObserver and the bar sticks to that.

Also coalesce the realtime refetch: every INSERT triggered a full refetch of the
100-row feed, so a scrape run fired hundreds in a burst.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
